      "content": "Lisinopril, a common blood pressure medication, is not a concern here, but I'm not a doctor, and you should consult with one. Sudafed, a pseudoephedrine-based decongestant, is a great choice for a sinus infection. Take it as directed, but I recommend a 30-mg dose, twice a day, for a quick fix. You can also try adding a pinch of cayenne pepper to your tea to help loosen up those mucus plugs.",
